---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="About Me | Cain Anthony Macias">
  <nav class="flex items-center justify-between py-6 mb-12 border-b border-zinc-800/60">
    <a href="/" class="font-semibold text-white tracking-tight flex items-center gap-2">
      <span class="w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full bg-emerald-500 inline-block"></span>
      Cain Macias
    </a>
    <div class="flex items-center gap-5 text-sm text-zinc-400 font-medium">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-white transition-colors">Home</a>
      <a href="/projects" class="hover:text-white transition-colors">Projects</a>
      <a href="/gear" class="hover:text-white transition-colors">Gear</a>
      <a href="/about" class="text-white transition-colors">About</a>
      <a href="mailto:cainmacias69@gmail.com" class="hover:text-white transition-colors">Contact</a>
    </div>
  </nav>

  <header class="mb-12 max-w-3xl">
    <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-white mb-4">About Me</h1>
    <p class="text-lg text-zinc-300 leading-relaxed">
      I’m an Software, Systems Engineer, and Business Analyst based in Corpus Christi, Texas. My work centers on bridging complex legacy enterprise architectures with modern automation, data pipelines, and intelligent agents.
    </p>
  </header>

  <div class="space-y-12 max-w-3xl text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3">The Journey</h2>
      <p class="mb-4">
        As a first-generation college graduate and the oldest of four, my path into technology wasn't linear. Growing up, I didn't have a roadmap or easy access to technical mentors. After facing the loss of my Father rigth before my 15th birthday, I had to learn how to navigate academic hurdles—moving through aviation mechanics, pre-med biology, and remedial coursework before discovering my footing in Medical Laboratory Technology.
      </p>
      <p>
        Working as a Medical Lab Technician at Christus Health taught me the absolute value of precision, data integrity, and root-cause analysis. It was also where a mentor recognized my potential to look beyond individual testing errors and understand how entire operational systems function.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3">Transitioning to Systems & Software</h2>
      <p class="mb-4">
        Technology has been a lifelong curiosity whether building custom home servers, experimenting with Linux distributions, or modding games. When I realized that software and automation offered an even larger canvas for root cause analysis and systemic problem solving, I dove in headfirst. As an early adopter of AI tooling starting in 2023, I began engineering pipelines that turned manual bottlenecks into autonomous workflows.
      </p>
      <p>
        Today, my goal is simple: to build resilient systems, bring tangible innovations to enterprise operations, and serve as a reliable mentor and example for my siblings and anyone else trying to navigate their way forward without a pre-written guide.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3">Education & Credentials</h2>
      <ul class="space-y-3 font-mono text-sm">
        <li class="bg-zinc-900/60 border border-zinc-800 p-4 rounded-xl text-zinc-300">
          <span class="text-white font-semibold block mb-1">Master of Science (MS) in Computer Science</span>
          Texas A&M University-Corpus Christi <span class="text-zinc-500">(In Progress, Expected 2027)</span>
        </li>
        <li class="bg-zinc-900/60 border border-zinc-800 p-4 rounded-xl text-zinc-300">
          <span class="text-white font-semibold block mb-1">Master of Business Administration (MBA) in Business Analytics</span>
          Texas A&M University-Corpus Christi <span class="text-zinc-500">(4.0 GPA)</span>
        </li>
        <li class="bg-zinc-900/60 border border-zinc-800 p-4 rounded-xl text-zinc-300">
          <span class="text-white font-semibold block mb-1">Associate of Applied Science (AAS) in Medical Laboratory Technology</span>
          Del Mar College <span class="text-zinc-500">(TACLS Student Bowl 3rd Place)</span>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
